PostgreSQL 16.15 (Ubuntu 16.15-0ubuntu0.24.04.1) on x86_64-pc-linux-gnu, compiled by gcc (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0, 64-bit

==============================================================================
SCENARIO 1a: Non-repeatable read under READ COMMITTED
A reads the same report twice. B changes it in between and commits.
==============================================================================
[  0.00s] A> BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL READ COMMITTED
           A  -> BEGIN
[  0.00s] A> SELECT recovered_bbls FROM accident WHERE report_number = 99990001
           A  -> 300.00
[  0.00s] B> UPDATE accident SET recovered_bbls = 350 WHERE report_number = 99990001
           B  -> UPDATE 1
[  0.00s] A> SELECT recovered_bbls FROM accident WHERE report_number = 99990001
           A  -> 350.00
[  0.00s] A> COMMIT
           A  -> COMMIT
RESULT: A saw 300.00 then 350.00 -> DIFFERENT values in one transaction

