SCENARIO 2a: Phantom read under READ COMMITTED
A counts an operator's open reports twice. B files a new report in between.
==============================================================================
[  0.00s] A> BEGIN ISOLATION LEVEL READ COMMITTED
           A  -> BEGIN
[  0.00s] A> SELECT COUNT(*) FROM accident WHERE operator_id = 31684 AND report_type = 'ORIGINAL'
           A  -> 4
[  0.00s] B> INSERT INTO accident (report_number, report_type, report_received_date, operator_id, on_off_shore, latitude, longitude, accident_datetime, pipe_facility_type, system_part_id, item_involved_id, commodity_subtype_id, release_type, unintentional_release_bbls, recovered_bbls, cause_detail_id, narrative) SELECT 99990020, 'ORIGINAL', report_received_date, operator_id, on_off_shore, latitude, longitude, accident_datetime, pipe_facility_type, system_part_id, item_involved_id, commodity_subtype_id, release_type, 10, 0, cause_detail_id, 'TEST REPORT - phantom demo' FROM accident WHERE report_number = 99990001
           B  -> INSERT 0 1
[  0.00s] A> SELECT COUNT(*) FROM accident WHERE operator_id = 31684 AND report_type = 'ORIGINAL'
           A  -> 5
[  0.00s] A> COMMIT
           A  -> COMMIT
RESULT: A counted 4 then 5 -> a new 'phantom' row appeared

