SCENARIO 6: FIX 3: one atomic UPDATE (no read-modify-write)
The addition happens inside the database: SET recovered = recovered + n.
B's UPDATE waits for A's row lock, then re-reads the latest committed value.
==============================================================================
[  0.00s] A> BEGIN
           A  -> BEGIN
[  0.00s] A> UPDATE accident SET recovered_bbls = recovered_bbls + 50 WHERE report_number = 99990001
           A  -> UPDATE 1
[  0.00s] B> BEGIN
           B  -> BEGIN
[  0.00s] B> UPDATE accident SET recovered_bbls = recovered_bbls + 30 WHERE report_number = 99990001
           (B is blocked, waiting for A's row lock)
[  1.50s] A> COMMIT
           A  -> COMMIT
           B  -> UPDATE 1
[  1.50s] B> COMMIT
           B  -> COMMIT
RESULT: recovered_bbls for 99990001 = 380.00  (CORRECT - both increments applied)

